.TH DR-CHARM 1 "2026-08-30" "dr-charm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dr-charm \- DragonRealms terminal client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -c | --config " " \fIPATH\fR ]
.RB [ -n | --no-log ]
.br
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -V | --version ]
.br
.B dr-charm
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dr-charm
authenticates to DragonRealms and renders a terminal interface.
The status bar shows connection and logging state. A disconnect remains visible
while the session closes or reconnects, and pane output can be scrolled.
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
.B Enter
Send the command line.
.TP
.B Ctrl-G
Open the command line in \fB$VISUAL\fR or \fB$EDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B Page Up, Page Down, Home, End
Scroll the focused pane.
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle panes with scrollable content.
.TP
.B Shift-Tab
Cycle panes in reverse.
.TP
.B F1
Show help.
.TP
.B F2
Toggle multi-pane and single-pane views.
.TP
.B F3
Select a theme.
.TP
.B F4
Toggle session logging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read credentials from PATH instead of the XDG default configuration file.
.TP
.BI -c " PATH"
Short form of \fB--config\fR.
.TP
.B --no-log
Disable the session transcript for this run. Logging is enabled by default.
.TP
.B -n
Short form of \fB--no-log\fR.
.TP
.B --version
Print the installed version without reading configuration or opening a network
connection.
.TP
.B -V
Short form of \fB--version\fR.
.TP
.B --help
Print help to standard output.
.TP
.B -h
Short form of \fB--help\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dr-charm/config.yaml
Default configuration file containing account credentials. A first run with no
configuration creates a commented template with owner-only permissions and exits.
When \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset, use \fI~/.config/dr-charm/config.yaml\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dr-charm/themes
Custom theme JSON files. When \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset, use
\fI~/.config/dr-charm/themes\fR.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/dr-charm/logs
Session transcripts. When \fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR is unset, use
\fI~/.local/state/dr-charm/logs\fR. New directories are owner-only and
closed logs are retained up to 30 files and 100 MiB as a soft limit.
.SH SECURITY
Configuration files and logs contain account data. New configuration files and
logs are readable only by their owner. Existing configuration modes are accepted.
The production binary does not read credential environment variables.
